(6336256, 936795, 112828, '<td valign="top">Since you seem to be curious as to what this is useful for, four things immediately come to mind:<br/> <br/>1. It''s pretty, display it as art.<br/> <br/>2. An example of hopper faced crystal growth, which is actually very rare.<br/> <br/>3. Melt it into a large thin plate, then do diamagnetic levitation.<br/> <br/>4. Demonstrations of expansion upon cooling, another rare property, shared with water, antimony and a few other things.</td>', 'Since you seem to be curious as to what this is useful for, four things immediately come to mind: 1. It''s pretty, display it as art. 2. An example of hopper faced crystal growth, which is actually very rare. 3. Melt it into a large thin plate, then do diamagnetic levitation. 4. Demonstrations of expansion upon cooling, another rare property, shared with water, antimony and a few other things.', '2011-02-28 23:52:25.000000', NULL, 0),
